 {"id": "ARM-1", "title": "P1 OWNER DECISION: the shipped default arm (jev) is the arm that cannot leave Pallet Town", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "DEFAULT_DECISION_MODE = 'jev' (cron_runner.py:115) — the hybrid, where System One decides and the LLM only repairs on escalation. Measured today and yesterday, same boot state: pure-LLM/controller 6/6 episodes to Route 1 (median 13.5 cycles) vs jev 0/5 (all censored at the 30-cycle cap); the 480-episode full run reached Route 1 once, around episode 202, and only because OR_JEV was 403-ing and the loop fell through to the controller — and never reached Viridian. Today the pure-LLM arm reached VIRIDIAN CITY (verifiable: RAM-read map name at ep021 cycle 2 of long_0927_llm) in 50 minutes. So the default we ship and point at as 'the result' is the arm that stalls. THIS ROW IS A DECISION, NOT A TASK: options are (a) flip the default to llm/system2 and treat the hybrid as the cost-optimisation experiment it was meant to be, (b) keep jev as default but make every benchmark report BOTH arms side by side so the default never again stands in for 'what the system does', or (c) hold until the continuation run (long_0927_llm2) gives a hold-rate for Viridian. Not acting without the owner's call.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:06:10.988705+00:00"}
 {"id": "BOOT-1", "title": "P1: the long-run driver's default boot state is a DIFFERENT map position than every measured baseline", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "long_run.py:47 hardcodes BOOT = data/boot.state. Probed with the project's own validator (long_run.probe_state): data/boot.state reads map 'Oak's Lab' (id 40) while data/baselines/base-1_boot.state reads 'Pallet Town' (id 0, md5 81e4ec4e8d1b62002bc78f619c5fc79c) — and Pallet Town is the state CTRL-WIN, DIST-1 and BASE-1 were all measured on. So a run launched the obvious way starts ~a whole map earlier and is silently incomparable to every number in data/baselines/, which is exactly the class of error that makes two runs look different for reasons that are not the agent. Compounding it: long_run.py passes no decision-mode flag to cron_runner.py (it invokes only --run-id, --cycles, --boot-state), so the arm a run used exists only in an ambient env var and is not recoverable from the run's own record. Worked around today by seeding long_run/<RUN_ID>_good.state from the canonical state and setting AIPP_DECISION_MODE explicitly — but that is operator discipline, not a property of the driver. Done-when: the driver takes the boot state and the decision mode as explicit arguments (or env with a loud default) and stamps BOTH into the run's status row and per-episode records, so a run cannot be launched from an unintended state or in an unrecorded arm.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:06:10.988705+00:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/ai-plays-poke-BOOT-1", "branch": "wt/BOOT-1", "worker_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "worker_provider": "xkiro", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-28T12:51:43", "commit_hash": "310c5f3", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "pending CI on push (see gh run list)", "worker_summary": "Boot-state stamp completed the row: long_run.py now records boot_state on the status row and every per-episode record; tests/test_long_run_boot.py 16 passed. Commit 05ae4c7 merged to main 310c5f3, pushed, rev-list 0.", "foreman_note": "Previous session merged the boot baseline (8e870a8); this tick landed the leftover worktree patch, merged, closed gitreins."}
-{"id": "EFF-1", "title": "P2: autonomy is 1.00 but the agent burned 8 episodes inside Red's House 1F — measure efficiency, not just escalation", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "The pure-LLM run long_0927_llm posted 594 decisions with 0 escalations and 0 errors, and the honest autonomy ratio reads 1.00 — while per-episode final maps show ep001-ep008 ALL ended in 'Red's House 1F', the starting house. Eight episodes (about 19 minutes) to walk out of a two-room building, with every decision counted as an unaided success. The autonomy metric is blind to this: a loop that re-decides the same wrong thing scores exactly as well as efficient progress. DIST-1 saw the mirror image (controller reaches Route 1 then wanders back; held only 4/6) and reported direction-locking at 41% of cycles. Done-when: runs report cycle-efficiency (decisions per map transition, and repeated-state/backtrack rate) alongside autonomy, so 'decided unaided' cannot be reported without 'and moved': the S0 baseline's 786.1 escalations-per-transition is the number this must be compared against.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:06:10.988705+00:00"}
+{"id": "EFF-1", "title": "P2: autonomy is 1.00 but the agent burned 8 episodes inside Red's House 1F — measure efficiency, not just escalation", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "The pure-LLM run long_0927_llm posted 594 decisions with 0 escalations and 0 errors, and the honest autonomy ratio reads 1.00 — while per-episode final maps show ep001-ep008 ALL ended in 'Red's House 1F', the starting house. Eight episodes (about 19 minutes) to walk out of a two-room building, with every decision counted as an unaided success. The autonomy metric is blind to this: a loop that re-decides the same wrong thing scores exactly as well as efficient progress. DIST-1 saw the mirror image (controller reaches Route 1 then wanders back; held only 4/6) and reported direction-locking at 41% of cycles. Done-when: runs report cycle-efficiency (decisions per map transition, and repeated-state/backtrack rate) alongside autonomy, so 'decided unaided' cannot be reported without 'and moved': the S0 baseline's 786.1 escalations-per-transition is the number this must be compared against.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T21:06:10.988705+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-07T07:55:00Z", "commit_hash": "19ef95113750d66ec5dc1699ad6d184372c7384d", "worker_status": "complete", "guard_result": "tier1 PASS 5/5 (worker standalone + foreman re-run: ruff+mypy+104 focused tests)", "ci_result": "pending CI run at tick write", "worker_summary": "Worker gpt-5.6-sol @ openai-codex: _autonomy_counters gains counted decisions_per_map_transition + backtrack_rate (map/tile repeated-state share) with evidence counts; run_autonomy block, summary tail (efficiency: X dec/map-transition, backtrack Y%, n/a forms) and BENCH-1 episode/comparison stamps carry them. RED-first: 7 new tests failed pre-impl. Post: 104 focused passed, ruff clean, mypy clean.", "foreman